0	144	Iliana Naydenova Ivanova (Bulgarian: Илиана Найденова Иванова; born 14 September 1975) is a Member of the European Court of Auditors since 2025.
145	272	She previously served as European Commissioner for Innovation, Research, Culture, Education and Youth between 2023 and 2024.



272	417	Early life and education
Ivanova graduated from foreign language high school Romain Rolland in her hometown where she studied French and English.
418	539	In 1998 she graduated with a bachelor's degree in International Economic Relations from the Economic University in Varna.
540	669	In 2004 Ivanova defended her master's thesis in International Finance at the Thunderbird School of Global Management, Arizona.



669	821	Early career
Ivanova worked as a coordinator for relations to international financial institutions at the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Forestry.



821	922	Member of the European Parliament
From 2009 to 2012, Ivanova was a Member of the European Parliament.
923	1235	During that period, she served as vice-chair of the Committee on Budgetary Control, Vice-chair of the Special Committee on the Economic, Financial and Social crisis, member of the Committee on the Int
1236	1353	In addition to her committee assignments, she was one of the  vice-chairs of the parliament's delegation to China.



1353	1462	Life after politics
As of the end of 2012, Ivanova has ceased all her political activities and affiliations.

1462	1554	Since 1 January 2013 Ivanova has been serving as a Member of the European Court of Auditors.
1555	1866	Ivanova was rapporteur for 27 audit reports, including topics such as regional development, cohesion, the Youth Unemployment Initiative and the Youth Guarantee, the European Digital Agenda and innovat
1867	1991	She was elected Dean of Chamber II, responsible for auditing structural policies, transport, for three consecutive mandates.
1992	2174	Since November 2022, she has been serving as Chair of the Audit quality control committee, with particular responsibility to oversee quality control of all RRF tasks across the ECA.

2174	2278	In June 2023, the Ivanova was nominated by the Bulgarian Government European Commissioner from Bulgaria.
2279	2501	On 28 June 2023, European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen proposed to the European Parliament and the Council to appoint Ivanova to the post of Commissioner for Innovation, Research, Culture
2502	2579	She was appointed as member of the European Commission on 19 September 2023.

2579	2741	Following her end of term as Commissioner, Iliana Ivanova was an appointed as Member of the European Court of Auditors from 1 January 2025 for a six-year mandate.
2742	2817	Ivanova was assigned to Chamber I: Sustainable use of natural resources.



